d "q-31517" :question/id #uuid "ba7f82da-4dd1-526e-9dfc-73ae8a9ea727" :question/math-academy-id "q-31517" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{{e}^{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{x{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31517/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31517"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336953/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "a079fdeb-a9f0-5c4c-a139-1bac32966fb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336953/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0296bdc1-e783-5066-818e-2de66b57a6b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336953/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-336953/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336953" :question/id #uuid "a37eeab6-798e-5dc0-b5e5-c7c2a03e11e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-336953" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{5{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{5{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[5{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]^{′}}{[2x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(10x+\\frac{1}{x})}{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336953/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336953"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336966/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1c737534-f1a8-5f82-b27d-20b6e4aa2185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336966/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3c64b3d3-ad22-5189-ad62-a6bd7048ff80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336966/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2ed7e69-bc95-5a14-b35c-9f5ca8714996" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336966/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-336966/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-336966/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336966" :question/id #uuid "d5abe0f2-94e8-57fc-a72a-431f152287b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-336966" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3/2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3/2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{3/2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]^{′}}{[{x}^{2}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{1}{x}}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3/2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{1}{x}]}^{′}}{[2x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{-1/2}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}}{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336966/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336966"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "c2d10e48-b44e-563c-aa37-d0dd37331a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "92f5bc3a-658c-564e-acaf-bc05f92a51cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "58426629-e3d7-5044-a7da-44aa577ceb96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "e05cbe87-e43b-51d4-bfe6-1eea9d5b0dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "73ade856-4ee3-526d-9f01-2d97b054d999" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "17ee673c-b7d2-578a-8bca-cc6d3c5f397f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114239/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-114239/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-114239/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-114239/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" "q-114239/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-114239/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114239" :question/id #uuid "9c771f81-c5b8-51aa-b04a-9b9d2e6048b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-114239" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{2}=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-x}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{2}]^{′}}{{[{e}^{-x}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{e}^{-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}} & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{[2x]^{′}}{[{e}^{-x}]^{′}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2}{-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =2{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{x} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114239/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "619df33a-7843-5c74-9da5-34186caf63b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2c451fa2-fc51-5189-9cb0-6f4c159f8621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "7b125944-1856-5ab1-beb7-434241d41c76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "bc33fa1a-f686-5b11-9603-3f8b71680708" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b136a36e-4ad7-53f5-9af2-e8d0cdf01a80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad13d99-b787-5977-a513-f2b4171b3171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31257/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-31257/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-31257/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-31257/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-31257/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-31257/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31257" :question/id #uuid "1f71e509-23a7-5349-9c54-3e2d5f1db3c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-31257" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+4x+3}{2x+3}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+4x+3}{2x+3} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\sqrt{x}+4x+3]^{′}}{[2x+3]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+4}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31257/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
